{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally in the UK", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Getting There", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Famous Structures > Buckingham Palace", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about directions to places in  a limited range of social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking for and Giving Directions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can ask for directions using modals like <span class=\"italic\">could</span> or <span class=\"italic\">can</span>:<br/><br>  <span class=\"italic\">Could you tell me how to get to \u2026 ?<br>Can you show me where we are on this map?<br>Can you tell me where \u2026 is?</span></span> <br><br>You can also ask for directions using Wh-question words: <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Where is the museum? </span><br/><br/>You can give directions using Imperatives:<br/><br><span class=\"italic\">Go straight down Upper Ground.<br>Then, walk through Jubilee Gardens.</span> <br><br> When a street changes name, you say \u201cit becomes\u201d. This is an example of the Simple Present tense. <br/><br><span class=\"italic\">Upper Grand becomes Belvedere Road.</span> <br><BR>There are many ways to say \u201cgo straight\u201d. Here are some of them:  <br><span class=\"italic\">Go straight ahead.<br>Go straight (up, down) \u2026 street.<br>Walk (up, down) \u2026 street.<br>Continue straight until \u2026 street.<br>Keep going straight till \u2026<br>Head up \u2026 street.</span> ", "type": "describer"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Travel & Transportation - The London Tube", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The London Tube, or the Underground, is the subway system of the City of London. It was built in 1863. It is the oldest subway system in the world.  It has 270 stations and covers a distance of 250 miles (400 kilometers). <br><br> Many people like to see the map of the London Tube. It is often printed on clothing and accessories.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob03img01.jpg", "type": "image"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the London Eye", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a very large wheel in London that you can sit in and go around", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to the London Eye. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you visit London.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the Underground", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the subway of London", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Here we call the subway the Underground.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the Tube", "type": "name"}, {"content": "another name for the subway of London", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  The Underground is also called the Tube.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "garden", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an area where you grow flowers or vegetables", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're on Upper Ground Street, beside Bernie Spain Gardens.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to become", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to turn into", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Upper Ground Street becomes Belvedere Road.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "closest", "type": "name"}, {"content": "located closer than any other thing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Where is the closest subway station?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online to find a map of the London Underground.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the questions in the table. Find the mystery stations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask your partner 3 more questions about the London Underground.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Complete the table.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cell